                <pb facs="0782" n="650" sameAs="frus:frus1926v01/pg650"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/7810: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-11-08T12:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 8,
                                1926—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received November 8—2:48
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>534. My 553 [<hi rendition="#italic">533</hi>], November 6, 11 a.m. Following
                    from American consul general, Hankow: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“November 6, 1 p.m. American naval radio from Kiukiang this morning
                            states city quiet and completely occupied by Southern troops, <pb
                                facs="0783" n="651" xml:id="pg651"/> practically all Northerners
                            having been evacuated down river. Japanese and American landing forces
                            withdrawn. Fighting reported in vicinity of Wusüeh.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
